  "paper": "paper_2",
  "question": {
    "html": "<p>An isotope of the radioactive element francium is francium-223 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left ( _{\\, \\, \\, 87}^{223}\\textrm{Fr} \\right )\"></span>.</p>\n<p>a. State what is meant by the term isotope.</p>\n<p>   [1]</p>\n<p>Francium-223 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left ( _{\\, \\, \\, 87}^{223}\\textrm{Fr} \\right )\"></span> decays into radium-223 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left ( _{\\, \\, \\, 88}^{223}\\textrm{Ra} \\right )\"></span>.</p>\n<p>b. Write an equation for this decay.</p>\n<p>   [3]</p>\n<p>Francium-223 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left ( _{\\, \\, \\, 87}^{223}\\textrm{Fr} \\right )\"></span> can decay into radon-215 <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\left ( _{\\, \\, \\, 86}^{215}\\textrm{Rn} \\right )\"></span> through a series of the following decays: <span class=\"math\" data-latex=\"\\alpha , \\: \\beta^{-} , \\: \\beta^{-} , \\: \\alpha , \\: \\beta^{-}\"></span>.</p>\n<p>c. On the diagram, draw five arrows to show how nucleon number and proton number changes during this decay.</p>\n\n<figure data-asset-id=\"fig_01\"><img alt=\"Source question diagram 1\" src=\"asset:fig_01\"/></figure>\n\n<p>  [3]</p>"
  },
